//
// SmolLM2-1.7B int4 (GGUF q4_0) compile-only smoke test: builds the bf16
// prefill kernels at SmolLM2 shapes plus the three int4 decode ELFs at gs=32
// through the AIR -> AIE -> aiecc -> Peano pipeline. No NPU dispatch, no
// HuggingFace weight download, no GGUF read.
//
// NOT CI-triggered by design: the filename intentionally OMITS "peano", so
// the CI peano suite (`lit --filter "peano"`) does not collect it — the
// llama32_1b_int4 compile lit is the int4 CI signal, and this example shares
// the same builders at a different gs. Kept so the example is runnable on
// demand:
//   lit -v programming_examples/llms/smollm2_1_7b_int4/run_npu2_compile.lit
//
// Gated on ryzen_ai_npu2 because the shared builders hardcode the AIE2P
// target; the compile does not touch the NPU device.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_compile
// RUN: cd test_peano_compile
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile compile PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: Compilation passed.
